{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback","id":1056070,"title":"Claws of the Unholy drawback","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-28T05:37:45-08:00","id":1056070,"title":"Claws of the Unholy drawback","content":"Hey, I was searching for the answer, but couldn't find it. I hope anybody didn't ask it already.<br /> How do you guys interpret the Claws of The Unholy Drawback?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Drawback: You may only use Claws of the Unholy while in<br /> frenzy or riding the wave. Once purchased, this modification<br /> is not optional; <b>the character manifests Claws of the Unholy<br /> any time she\u2019s frenzied</b>. </div> </div> </div>1. Frenzy. You MUST spend Vitae to activate Claws of the Unholy, since it's &quot;<b>ANY time she's frenzied</b>&quot;<br /> 2. Frenzy. Nothing happens, when you spend vitae on Unnatural Aspect you cannot activate any talons, fangs, claws which do bashing or lethal damage only the aggravated unholy version.<br /> <br /> The 1st interpretation seems to look good for most of the Gangrel since the Beast wants to kill anyway, but it looks kinda funny in Ordo Dracul, because experienced Dragons who Mastered all the Coils of the Wyrm are more stoic and could want to ride the wave to achieve different goals with frenzy.<br /> <br /> What do you think? I know that the ST can pick his or her version, but I like to keep the rules as written in terms of the game mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 02-28-2017, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:15:14-08:00","id":1056094,"title":"","content":"Every time they enter frenzy or ride the wave they have the claws that do aggravated damage appear. If someone wants to master the mystery of the wyrm and use frenzy for other benefits besides ripping people to shreds and not having an automatic visual indicator they are in frenzy then they should think twice about purchasing this merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-28-2017, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:59:30-08:00","id":1056114,"title":"","content":"Conversely, I always read it as the second one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:10:45-08:00","id":1056121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056094#post1056094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time they enter frenzy or ride the wave they have the claws that do aggravated damage appear. If someone wants to master the mystery of the wyrm and use frenzy for other benefits besides ripping people to shreds and not having an automatic visual indicator they are in frenzy then they should think twice about purchasing this merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the first interpretation is correct. From an in character perspective it'd be unwise to relinquish control of a particular body transformation to the Beast and expect to reign it in without additional effort.<br /> <br /> Speaking of additional effort to overcome drawbacks, that's the Defiants' thing. It is very likely a Gangrel Dragon somewhere has a Devotion of an appropriate level of the Mystery of the Wyrm and Protean that allows getting around this drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:18:20-08:00","id":1056124,"title":"","content":"It doesn't gel with the rest of the merit though. It says &quot;When wielding claws borne of Unnatural Aspect while in frenzy, this Merit takes effect.&quot; If they popped out any time you frenzy, it would just say &quot;when in frenzy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:29:12-08:00","id":1056130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056124#post1056124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't gel with the rest of the merit though. It says &quot;When wielding claws borne of Unnatural Aspect while in frenzy, this Merit takes effect.&quot; If they popped out any time you frenzy, it would just say &quot;when in frenzy&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see how you are reading it and understand your mistake. The reason it doesn't say &quot;when in frenzy&quot; even though that would save word count is that it's possible to attack without claws while in frenzy. If it merely said &quot;when in frenzy&quot; you could elbow and bite for Aggravated damage while in frenzy., thus the qualifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-28-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:36:08-08:00","id":1056132,"title":"","content":"The merit DOES say that. It's expressly labeled as a drawback to the merit. If you aren't in frenzy, you can choose whether or not you manifest the claws capable of inflicting aggravated when you exhibit claws. If you enter frenzy, you don't get to choose. The claws (and attendant vitae expenditure) that do aggravated damage always appear. Whether or not you can retract them if you exercise a degree of control over frenzy or they have to remain visible is up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:38:13-08:00","id":1056134,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how a +0 aggravated modifier specifically to claws would allow for aggravated bites and elbow strikes.<br /> <br /> Also Unnatural Aspect costs 2 vitae to activate, not one. You need to have Predatory Aspect up to use it. Which raises questions about how this is supposed to work for blood potency one vampires, as well as for vampires who don't have enough vitae to spend.<br /> <br /> Also also this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056132#post1056132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you aren't in frenzy, you can choose whether or not you manifest the claws capable of inflicting aggravated when you exhibit claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is just flat-out wrong. &quot;You may only use Claws of the Unholy while in frenzy or riding the wave.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-28-2017, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:06:35-08:00","id":1056137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056134#post1056134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how a +0 aggravated modifier specifically to claws would allow for aggravated bites and elbow strikes. <br /> <br /> Also Unnatural Aspect costs 2 vitae to activate, not one. You need to have Predatory Aspect up to use it. Which raises questions about how this is supposed to work for blood potency one vampires, as well as for vampires who don't have enough vitae to spend.<br /> <br /> Also also this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is just flat-out wrong. &quot;You may only use Claws of the Unholy while in frenzy or riding the wave.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I no longer think you are mistaken. Obviously you are defending an incorrect reading of the rules on purpose. The mental backflip needed to in one post point out the 3rd sentence of the merit as too wordy to allow a natural reading as a descriptive line stating the merit's intent before the 4th sentence, and in your next post deny description is needed because the 4th sentence contains the whole of the mechanics. <br /> <br /> Please feel free to houserule as you please, but the rules as written are very clear, and only an outlier situation brings any questions. <br /> <br /> By the way, the question about lacking Vitae is good and would be up to storyteller discretion because it isn't covered. I do think a ruling that would be consistent with RAW would be sprouting aforementioned Unholy Claw as soon as the Vitae can be spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-28-2017, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:06:49-08:00","id":1056139,"title":"","content":"If you have claws from Unnatural Aspect active when you frenzy, they become Claws of the Unholy. You have no say in the matter.<br /> <br /> If you do not have Unnatural Aspect active when you frenzy, then you do not get Claws of the Unholy unless you use Unnatural Aspect to get claws; something a frenzying Gangrel may well do depending on the goal.<br /> <br /> If your Unnatural Aspect is not claws, then you do not get Claws of the Unholy. People seem to forget that it has other options, and that you can change what option you have with some effort. Wings would be much better if you suspect you'll need to run like hell instead of fight your way out, frenzy or not.<br /> <br /> Basically, you cannot use Barbed Hands (+grapple), Hooked Hands (tunneling; another power for escaping), or Horrid Talons(armor piercing) in frenzy anymore. All three of these turn into Claws of the Unholy while frenzying.<br /> <br /> Though technically Horrid Talons can be fangs, so if you picked the fang option I'd still let you keep it in frenzy. CotU specifically refers to claws.<br /> <br /> I don't think it forces you to use Unnatural Aspect. That doesn't follow the text very well, and it would be absolutely silly considering Unnatural Aspect doesn't always give you claws (and therefore doesn't always give you CotU).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:15:49-08:00","id":1056146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056137#post1056137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I no longer think you are mistaken. Obviously you are defending an incorrect reading of the rules on purpose. The mental backflip needed to in one post point out the 3rd sentence of the merit as too wordy to allow a natural reading as a descriptive line stating the merit's intent before the 4th sentence, and in your next post deny description is needed because the 4th sentence contains the whole of the mechanics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What on earth are you talking about? It's not a mental backflip at all. The line works perfectly well as-written because the preceding sentence already said that you needed claws active. My suggestion as to how the merit would read if it meant the interpretation you are proposing would obviously change the second line to something like &quot;When in frenzy, the vampire manifests +0 aggravated claws.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:23:15-08:00","id":1056152,"title":"","content":"I never said it would grant aggravated damage to bites or elbow strikes. If a player of mine wanted to apply it to horns or tusks they have from their predatory aspect (because they ate a wild hog for instance) I'd permit it personally but the merit itself says claws. <br /> <br /> I said the attendant vitae cost, not one vitae.<br /> <br /> As for its usefulness to BP 1 characters, there's two routes, <br /> 1. BP 1 characters can't use it.<br /> 2. BP 1 characters can use it by spending the vitae over multiple turns and gain the benefit once it's paid for vitae wise.<br /> <br /> The merit enhances a specific type of predatory aspect. (Claws) A character is capable of having more than one predatory aspect at a time. If they want the aggravated damage claws, they have to put themselves or be triggered into frenzy. But if they want the claws in order to do something else, (for instance climb over a 15 ft high wooden fence) they can still grow them without having to enter frenzy. They just won't get the claws that do aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-28-2017, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:26:34-08:00","id":1056153,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> You are reading it as a modification of an existing ability, not adding an ability. I would agree with that reading except for the last two sentences of the merit, which make it clear that while in frenzy the Unnatural Aspect is always claws, and always manifest. Does this imply the vampire could hypothetically have a non-frenzy Unnatural Aspect which they change out of when in frenzy? I'd say yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:30:32-08:00","id":1056155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056152#post1056152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said it would grant aggravated damage to bites or elbow strikes</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Pale_Crusader suggested that that would be the case if the line detailing when the merit activated didn't specify needing the claws active. Which I still don't understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:32:26-08:00","id":1056158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056153#post1056153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> You are reading it as a modification of an existing ability, not adding an ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're reading it as a modification because <b>that is literally what the merit calls itself in the very line you are referring to.<br /> <br /> &quot;</b>Once purchased, this <b>modification</b> is not optional; the character manifests Claws of the Unholy any time she\u2019s frenzied.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I stand by my assertion that this line does not mean what you think it does. It means that if the <i>two</i> prerequisites for use (being both in frenzy and having the claws active) are <i>both</i> present, <i>then</i> the vampire doesn't get a say in whether it activates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-28-2017, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:57:33-08:00","id":1056166,"title":"","content":"IMHO, because of:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><b>When wielding claws</b><br /> borne of Unnatural Aspect <b>while in frenzy</b>, this Merit <b>takes effect</b></span></span> </div> </div> </div>the 2nd interpretation is correct (like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> wrote) , but many people have a different point of view. I understand that the merit has a flaw, but the question is, <b>how severe the drawback is</b>?<br /> A clever Dragon could use subterfuge skills to somehow hide that he is in frenzy in the Elysium, but having his claws all the time would be offensive and against the rules- to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:01:13-08:00","id":1056171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056158#post1056158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're reading it as a modification because <b>that is literally what the merit calls itself in the very line you are referring to.<br /> <br /> &quot;</b>Once purchased, this <b>modification</b> is not optional; the character manifests Claws of the Unholy any time she\u2019s frenzied.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I stand by my assertion that this line does not mean what you think it does. It means that if the <i>two</i> prerequisites for use (being both in frenzy and having the claws active) are <i>both</i> present, <i>then</i> the vampire doesn't get a say in whether it activates.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Elfive <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I see you can disagree about how I said something without refuting my point that it is an addition of an ability. I wasn't addressing you because I don't believe you can be changed in your stance regardless of clear evidence and indeed expect you to claim all those that disagree with you have no valid points due to black/white thinking on your part. I have put this in spoilers because addressing you isn't productive towards helping people. Also if you read more finely you'd notice I used the word ability, not power nor Discipline, and that was deliberate because I was aware it's a modification of a power.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be clear it is a modification that adds an ability to Unnatural Aspect and yes it does use the word &quot;modification&quot;. It doesn't globally change the power, and doesn't have a prerequisite that the non-frenzy Unnatural Aspect be claws, but does say <br /> :&quot;the character manifests Claws of the Unholy any time she\u2019s frenzied.&quot; Which means claws of the unholy are additional ability of the Unnatural Aspect that manifest while in frenzy, which is the simplest most natural reading of the rules, and is indeed the first interpretation the original post had. The alterative is far more convoluted.<br /> <br /> Please remember the rules are written in natural language, not technical language","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-28-2017, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:08:47-08:00","id":1056177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056166#post1056166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, because of:<br /> <br /> the 2nd interpretation is correct (like <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> wrote) , but many people have a different point of view. I understand that the merit has a flaw, but the question is, <b>how severe the drawback is</b>?<br /> A clever Dragon could use subterfuge skills to somehow hide that he is in frenzy in the Elysium, but having his claws all the time would be offensive and against the rules- to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>A clever Dragon wouldn't be making a habit of going to elysium in frenzy in the first place because that is literally begging to be put to final death or worse getting their blood potency stripped to zero indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:13:55-08:00","id":1056179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056177#post1056177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A clever Dragon wouldn't be making a habit of going to elysium in frenzy in the first place because that is literally begging to be put to final death or worse getting their blood potency stripped to zero indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup you're right, it's just an example. I just want to emphasize that the frenzy can be used to lash out in a conversation. Elysium seems too be to risky in most of the cases, so it isn't a good habit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:14:57-08:00","id":1056180,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is closer to the 2nd one, and I never thought it would be in question. After reading this thread, I can understand why you might lean to the 1st.<br /> <br /> I've always read Claws of the Unholy as:<br /> Merit - you do aggravated damage when you pop claw in frenzy<br /> Drawback - you can only ever do aggravated damage when you pop claw in frenzy<br /> <br /> A frenzied Gangrel will likely pop claw instantly and destroy their enemy if given a chance. For those who say a BP 1 Gangrel can't pop claw right away, then they would spend the two vitae over two turns while pursuing their prey in other ways. If the Gangrel doesn't have the vitae for it, he/she probably won't do it. If Riding the Wave, the player can choose whether to pop claw at all. But if they DO pop claw, they better be prepared to bring someone to final death.<br /> <br /> That's its own drawback - you are going to Kill whatever you're fighting, and you've permanently lost the ability to claw someone into torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:27:02-08:00","id":1056188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056180#post1056180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation is closer to the 2nd one, and I never thought it would be in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a similar feeling. A friend of mine had a different interpretation (the 1st one), so I decided to ask how you guys interpret the rules. Opinions are quite divided and it isn't clear what was the merit intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:27:30-08:00","id":1056189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056171#post1056171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please remember the rules are written in natural language, not technical language</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the one taking the last line of the merit as gospel and ignoring the bit that is actually supposed to explain what it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:36:40-08:00","id":1056195,"title":"","content":"This debate could be a matter of emphasis in the reading. Both sides seem to think it is clear and yet maintain mutually exclusive views. For the reasons I mentioned, I still stand by my reading but would like to hear the developer's intent in case there is a more elegant/consistent/balanced way to handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-28-2017, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:39:57-08:00","id":1056198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056195#post1056195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This debate could be a matter of emphasis in the reading. Both sides seem to think it is clear and yet maintain mutally-exclusive views. For the reasons I mentioned, I still stand bu my reading but would like to hear the developer's intent in case there is a more elegant/consistent/balanced way to handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The developer's answer would be the best option. For me both interpretations seem reasonable (I have a feeling that 2nd is correct). It is a matter of choice, but I like to house rule as little as possible. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 02-28-2017, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:52:10-08:00","id":1056204,"title":"","content":"It never even occurred to me that this would be interpreted in any way other than 1. Like, &quot;the character manifests Claws of the Unholy any time she\u2019s frenzied&quot; seems completely unambiguous to me. You're in Frenzy? Then you manifest Claws of the Unholy. The &quot;When wielding claws borne of Unnatural Aspect while in frenzy, this Merit takes effect&quot; part, then, establishes the Vitae cost. Between these two sentences, the natural interpretation to me seems to be that every time a vampire with this Merit enters Frenzy, she must activate Unnatural Aspect for 2 Vitae (spending it over multiple turns if necessary, and presumably falling into Torpor if she doesn't have enough Vitae to pay for it, just like when you don't have enough Vitae to heal all of your injuries during daysleep). When she does this, her claws have a damage modifier of 0A instead of their normal modifier. The only question this interpretation leaves in my mind is what happens if her Unnatural Aspect isn't claws, and my ruling on that is, you would then be unable to access the normal +2L AP2 claws out of Frenzy and be unable to access your wings or whatever in Frenzy.<br /> <br /> Upon reading others' interpretations, I can see now how it could be read as 2. Still seems wrong to me, as if you are in Frenzy and don't activate Unnatural Aspect, that would be a time you frenzied and didn't manifest Claws of the Unholy, which seems to be contrary to the drawback to me, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:58:30-08:00","id":1056210,"title":"","content":"Given that the number one cause of frenzy is starvation, I think forcing vampires into torpor if they can't pay for it would result in vampires losing control only to comically fall flat on their face to be far too frequent an occurrence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:00:25-08:00","id":1056212,"title":"","content":"My reading is/was #1 and like others here, I didn't think there could be a different interpretation.<br /> How is it a drawback if you get to choose beforehand whether you're going to pop them or not? It is certainly a drawback if &quot;the Character manifests Claws of the Unholy any time she's frenzied.&quot; As for activation cost, The Beast can do lots of crazy things that aren't usually an option so dumping a burst of Vitae doesn't seem out of line. If the char doesn't contain enough Vitae atm, I would at least have them Frenzy till it ends, then maybe fall into Torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:00:56-08:00","id":1056213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056198#post1056198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The developer's answer would be the best option. For me both interpretations seem reasonable (I have a feeling that 2nd is correct). It is a matter of choice, but I like to house rule as little as possible. <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> would actually be the one to ask, as I'm pretty sure he wrote it. That said, I'm not a fan of relying on word of writer or word of developer for these interpretations. Apart from the fact that they have other things to do with their lives than settle our rules disputes, I hold strongly to the idea of death of the author. Knowing a writer or developer's intent can provide insight, which might help us form our own interpretations, but ultimately we should still interpret the work ourselves. I feel like we've been kind of spoiled by how active the writers and developers are on these forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:02:42-08:00","id":1056215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056210#post1056210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the number one cause of frenzy is starvation, I think forcing vampires into torpor if they can't pay for it would result in vampires losing control only to comically fall flat on their face to be far too frequent an occurrence.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience if hunger Frenzy is going to happen, it usually happens before the Vampire hits 1 Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:03:53-08:00","id":1056217,"title":"","content":"My assumption was that frequently one would fall into frenzy in the middle of a fight when they were already out, thus causing the fight to suddenly become a lot more lethal. <br /> <br /> Drawbacks don't always need to be a kick in the teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:04:02-08:00","id":1056218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056215#post1056215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my experience if hunger Frenzy is going to happen, it usually happens before the Vampire hits 1 Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly a drawback. It makes 3 Vitae functionally equivalent to someone without this Merit hitting 1.<br /> It's still a very worthy trade to always have an Agg weapon on tap that can't ever be taken away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 02-28-2017, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:06:53-08:00","id":1056220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056213#post1056213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> would actually be the one to ask, as I'm pretty sure he wrote it. That said, I'm not a fan of relying on word of writer or word of developer for these interpretations. Apart from the fact that they have other things to do with their lives than settle our rules disputes, I hold strongly to the idea of death of the author. Knowing a writer or developer's intent can provide insight, which might help us form our own interpretations, but ultimately we should still interpret the work ourselves. I feel like we've been kind of spoiled by how active the writers and developers are on these forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, you're right, but I have asked him a question few weeks ago about Obtenebration already and didn't want to be annoying. He we will think I play Dungeon and Dragons Chronicles of Darkness or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:24:36-08:00","id":1056236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056213#post1056213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> would actually be the one to ask, as I'm pretty sure he wrote it. That said, I'm not a fan of relying on word of writer or word of developer for these interpretations. Apart from the fact that they have other things to do with their lives than settle our rules disputes, I hold strongly to the idea of death of the author. Knowing a writer or developer's intent can provide insight, which might help us form our own interpretations, but ultimately we should still interpret the work ourselves. I feel like we've been kind of spoiled by how active the writers and developers are on these forums.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I also believe in Death of the Author, Death of the Author in this case would be &quot;do what works at your table.&quot; People who prefer option 1 can use option 1, people who prefer option 2 can use option 2. Which is the default setting of most rules in an RPG.<br /> <br /> This thread specifically exists to hem and haw about the actual, &quot;canonical&quot; (read: writers') interpretation of the rule. Which would mean, at their convenience, Rose or David's interpretation.<br /> <br /> And to be fair, even if Rose or David told me that option 1 was the correct, canonical answer, I would still probably go with option 2 at my table, because the Golden Rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:33:36-08:00","id":1056241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056236#post1056236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I also believe in Death of the Author, Death of the Author in this case would be &quot;do what works at your table.&quot; People who prefer option 1 can use option 1, people who prefer option 2 can use option 2. Which is the default setting of most rules in an RPG.<br /> <br /> This thread specifically exists to hem and haw about the actual, &quot;canonical&quot; (read: writers') interpretation of the rule. Which would mean, at their convenience, Rose or David's interpretation.<br /> <br /> And to be fair, even if Rose or David told me that option 1 was the correct, canonical answer, I would still probably go with option 2 at my table, because the Golden Rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I do it differently. I don't like the golden rule and love clear rules. I enjoy such game more, but I know that the developers have more things to do than answering my questions. Anyways thank you all for your opinions I appreciate it. If Rose or David gives an answer, I'll hapilly change my mind and change the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 02-28-2017, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:40:25-08:00","id":1056244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056236#post1056236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I also believe in Death of the Author, Death of the Author in this case would be &amp;quot;do what works at your table.&amp;quot; People who prefer option 1 can use option 1, people who prefer option 2 can use option 2. Which is the default setting of most rules in an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which I think we've established is the &quot;real&quot; answer, we're just discussing our reasoning for our own interpretations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056236#post1056236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread specifically exists to hem and haw about the actual, &amp;quot;canonical&amp;quot; (read: writers') interpretation of the rule. Which would mean, at their convenience, Rose or David's interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which is why I say I think the writer and developer activity on these boards has spoiled us. A thread like this should exist to discuss our interpretations and reasoning for those interpretations, to give people an opportunity to examine the rules from others' perspectives, and thereby help us develop better-informed interpretations. Even if we walk away not having changed our opinions, we still walk away with a deeper understanding of the rules. I, for example, had no idea 2 was even an interpretation people would have, and although I remain unconvinced it is the &quot;right&quot; interpretation for my game, my understanding of the rule is still expanded. In this model of discussion, writer/developer intent isn't the goal of the discussion, merely one more perspective to consider and expand our understanding. Nice to have if they are inclined to chime in, not something we tag them in to settle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056236#post1056236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to be fair, even if Rose or David told me that option 1 was the correct, canonical answer, I would still probably go with option 2 at my table, because the Golden Rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. Which is part of why I think it's a little silly that the community as a whole is so invested in seeking out writer/developer input.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:01:40-08:00","id":1056256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056244#post1056244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course. Which is part of why I think it's a little silly that the community as a whole is so invested in seeking out writer/developer input.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it's like playing a game of chess and making moves that the players agree on, so it's little silly to do exactly the opposite and don't ask. It's like cooking without the recipe and without measuring the exact weight. In the end the most important think is to have fun and enjoy your game, so everyone should play how he or she likes. In everyday life I do a lot of math, coding etc., so I like precision in everything I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 02-28-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:47:50-08:00","id":1056285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056256#post1056256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it's like playing a game of chess and making moves that the players agree on, so it's little silly to do exactly the opposite and don't ask. It's like cooking without the recipe and without measuring the exact weight. In the end the most important think is to have fun and enjoy your game, so everyone should play how he or she likes. In everyday life I do a lot of math, coding etc., so I like precision in everything I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precision is important, of course - once you decide how you're going to rule, you should rule consistently. But as long as everyone at your table knows and is playing by the same rules, it doesn't matter if those rules are different from the ones everyone at my table are playing by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:11:47-08:00","id":1056292,"title":"","content":"After mulling it over I've come to the conclusion that if the drawback was that it sucked 2 vitae out of you every time you entered frenzy it would explicitly <i>say that</i>. <br /> <br /> So either it only happens if you have the claws out. or it activates for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:12:56-08:00","id":1056294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056285#post1056285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precision is important, of course - once you decide how you're going to rule, you should rule consistently. But as long as everyone at your table knows and is playing by the same rules, it doesn't matter if those rules are different from the ones everyone at my table are playing by.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a point here, it doesn't matter whose the rules are, but I feel better not to house rule if only I can find out what was the purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After mulling it over I've come to the conclusion that if the drawback was that it sucked 2 vitae out of you every time you entered frenzy it would explicitly <i>say that</i>. <br /> <br /> So either it only happens if you have the claws out. or it activates for free </div> </div> </div> I have the same feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:06:05-08:00","id":1056360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056292#post1056292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After mulling it over I've come to the conclusion that if the drawback was that it sucked 2 vitae out of you every time you entered frenzy it would explicitly <i>say that</i>.<br /> <br /> So either it only happens if you have the claws out. or it activates for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's highly abusable though unless you say it only activates for free if the frenzy is actually unintentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:10:44-08:00","id":1056363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056360#post1056360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's highly abusable though unless you say it only activates for free if the frenzy is actually unintentional.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is why I think that's why it isn't the intention. I really, really think the drawback to the merit is exactly the same as the benefit - when you try to kill something, you will kill it. No going back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T17:27:37-08:00","id":1056387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056360#post1056360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's highly abusable though unless you say it only activates for free if the frenzy is actually unintentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess he wanted to emphasize that the developers would mention about the additional cost of frenzy.Since they didn't there are two possible options- it is activated when you use the discipline while in frenzy(2nd interpretation) or it is free (highly unlikely).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:24:22-08:00","id":1056467,"title":"","content":"For those that say the drawback if it doesn't force you to spend Vitae is too low:<br /> <br /> Do consider that the drawback for Undead Menses is &quot;must identify as female.&quot;<br /> <br /> Drawbacks aren't necessarily drawbacks in OPP books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:54:33-08:00","id":1056494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056467#post1056467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those that say the drawback if it doesn't force you to spend Vitae is too low:<br /> <br /> Do consider that the drawback for Undead Menses is &quot;must identify as female.&quot;<br /> <br /> Drawbacks aren't necessarily drawbacks in OPP books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the drawback isn't enough of a drawback under interpretation 2. I just think the drawback doesn't do what it says it does under interpretation 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:28:39-08:00","id":1056518,"title":"","content":"The drawback says the <i>modification </i>isn't optional, not that the claws aren't.<br /> <br /> &quot;The character manifests Claws of the Unholy any time she\u2019s frenzied&quot; <i>doesn't mean</i> &quot;The character manifests Claws of the Unholy at the moment she enters frenzy.&quot; It just means that the character doesn't get a choice about it if the <i>two </i>conditions <i>clearly spelled out in the first paragraph</i> are present.<br /> <br /> Claws of the unholy is explicitly a <i>modification</i> to a discipline that the merit is <i>never</i> mentioned to force you to activate.<br /> <br /> And the last line doesn't mention needing the discipline active because <i>that has already been established.</i><br /> <br /> The drawback may not do what it says it does under interpretation 2, but the <i>merit</i> doesn't do what it says it does under interpretation 1.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-01-2017, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T02:22:13-08:00","id":1056544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056518#post1056518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The drawback says the <i>modification </i>isn't optional, not that the claws aren't.<br /> <br /> &quot;The character manifests Claws of the Unholy any time she\u2019s frenzied&quot; <i>doesn't mean</i> &quot;The character manifests Claws of the Unholy at the moment she enters frenzy.&quot; It just means that the character doesn't get a choice about it if the <i>two </i>conditions <i>clearly spelled out in the first paragraph</i> are present.<br /> <br /> Claws of the unholy is explicitly a <i>modification</i> to a discipline that the merit is <i>never</i> mentioned to force you to activate.<br /> <br /> And the last line doesn't mention needing the discipline active because <i>that has already been established.</i><br /> <br /> The drawback may not do what it says it does under interpretation 2, but the <i>merit</i> doesn't do what it says it does under interpretation 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree, but I guess that the supporters of the 1st interpretation won't change their mind unless we see the developers intention. In the end a ST can choose what suits him or her. Both interpretations seem reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T02:26:52-08:00","id":1056545,"title":"","content":"Are they though? &quot;When X, if Y, Z&quot; doesn't logically equate to &quot;When Y, X and Z&quot; no matter how you twist it.<br /> <br /> The first paragraph of the merit, the one that tells you what it <i>actually does,</i> takes precedence. I agree that the drawback <i>could </i>be read two ways, but the context, that the writer is assuming you've read the first paragraph, makes it absolutely clear which one we're supposed to take it as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-01-2017, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T02:45:48-08:00","id":1056551,"title":"","content":"It's the fourth page of this thread and I don't think (but I can have missed it) that anyone has claimed that the Merit simply contradicts itself. There are two absolute statements in the text and the entire argument seems to be which one takes priority over the other. After over three pages of arguing back and forth I'm pretty sure it's not going to get solved unless a dev wants to clarify the intent. I think it's better to just pick one interpretation (whichever is more fitting for your Chronicle since the largest drawback anyway is the damage) and just stick with it for the sake of consistence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T03:00:24-08:00","id":1056561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056551#post1056551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the fourth page of this thread and I don't think (but I can have missed it) that anyone has claimed that the Merit simply contradicts itself. There are two absolute statements in the text and the entire argument seems to be which one takes priority over the other. After over three pages of arguing back and forth I'm pretty sure it's not going to get solved unless a dev wants to clarify the intent. I think it's better to just pick one interpretation (whichever is more fitting for your Chronicle since the largest drawback anyway is the damage) and just stick with it for the sake of consistence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we won't settle anything without a clarification, so until then anyone picks what suits him or her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T03:31:46-08:00","id":1056562,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go out on a limb and suggest that the merit in its entirety is a drawback! 2L &gt; 0A!! Don't believe the hype!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:27:01-08:00","id":1056627,"title":"","content":"Vampires frenzy on more than just enemies.<br /> Careful vampires who frenzy without CotU might be able to maintain the Masquerade as someone on bath salts or PCP - not obvious monsters that leave supernatural wound marks on victims and the environment for hunters to find.<br /> Wave-riders can use tools in frenzy that CotU wielders cannot.<br /> <br /> I favor the interpretation: When manifesting claws, if you are in frenzy, you instead manifest CotU. There seems to me plenty of other drawbacks beyond trying to shoehorn in auto-Vitae expenditures and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:36:40-08:00","id":1056647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056562#post1056562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go out on a limb and suggest that the merit in its entirety is a drawback! 2L &gt; 0A!! Don't believe the hype!</div> </div> </div> </div>Laughs out loud! Yeah unless murdering people while in Frenzy instead of merely mauling them is your thing, Aggravated Damage isn't that good. Of course if you are into being a murderer that kills while in fits of rage, it's amazing because it skips the bleeding out or torpor stages of the death, making a coup de grace unneeded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-01-2017, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:44:17-08:00","id":1056650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056647#post1056647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Laughs out loud! Yeah unless murdering people while in Frenzy instead of merely mauling them is your thing, Aggravated Damage isn't that good. Of course if you are into being a murderer that kills while in fits of rage, it's amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is exactly why the merit is its own drawback.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd probably only take Claws of the Unholy so I could feel like a classic VtM Gangrel/1st ed VtR Gangrel again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","user":"RomulusGloriosus","date":".  sake of conversation 03-01-2017, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T09:20:58-08:00","id":1056662,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that dealing aggravated damages is not as easy as in vtm anymore. Now is a much better comproimise to me. Aggravated damages means final death in just one life bar and before was possible for quite Everyone to deal aggravated with protean 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T09:33:19-08:00","id":1056664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056662#post1056662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad that dealing aggravated damages is not as easy as in vtm anymore. Now is a much better comproimise to me. Aggravated damages means final death in just one life bar and before was possible for quite Everyone to deal aggravated with protean 2.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. While I played a Gangrel in VtM for a long time, and Fortitude (Resilience) kind of off-sets the proliferation of Aggravated Damage, but More Lethal means more ways to get knocked into torpor, which I kind of see as the &quot;usual&quot; way a Vampire dies, given how many times &quot;DRACULA IS BACK FROM THE DEAD!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:54:32-08:00","id":1056854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1056562#post1056562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go out on a limb and suggest that the merit in its entirety is a drawback! 2L &gt; 0A!! Don't believe the hype!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well in many cases, maybe even most of them you're right, but aggravated damage means overcoming most of the armor and stop healing via vitae during the combat,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 03-02-2017, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T03:32:26-08:00","id":1057037,"title":"","content":"Agg claws do have a very specific use, and, honestly, I don't feel like its to bypass armor or healing. Unless you're fighting a werewolf (in which case, get silver weapons, or even silver punching daggers), I find that 2L generally is faster driving a vampire to torpor even with healing, and the default claws come with Armor Piercing 2, shredding through regular armor as it is. You have to remember that, if a vampire isn't spending vitae to heal, its spending it to deal more damage to you, which has an end result of not helping that much. Plus, dealing lethal damage has the upside of being able to frenzy in combat for the dice boost / mind control protection without needing to Final Death any vampires you fight. And, yes, always having agg claws in a frenzy is a major drawback. It means that any fight you get into is either going to be 1) handicapped, or 2) going for the Final Death of your opponent. That kind of severely limits one's options, I find.<br /> <br /> In the end, I found the best use of agg claws is because of the strix. Agg claws are one of the few ways to directly injure one of the Owls of Dis. Outside of that? I feel like its actually more limiting that effective. That said, agg claws do make good threats - even if one is sure they can survive an attack against someone with the claws, no one wants to spend the time healing that damage, nor do they want the acompanying scars.<br /> <br /> Honestly, agg claws are probably a strong reason why Gangrel are called Savages. Its the &quot;everything looks like a nail&quot; problem you need to solve with absolute finality. That implies a certian level of inherant violence any interaction with the agg claw Gangrel comes with that other disciplines don't bring to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-02-2017, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:17:15-08:00","id":1057249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1057037#post1057037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, agg claws are probably a strong reason why Gangrel are called Savages. Its the &quot;everything looks like a nail&quot; problem you need to solve with absolute finality. That implies a certian level of inherant violence any interaction with the agg claw Gangrel comes with that other disciplines don't bring to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. I played a Gangrel for a very long time in a VtM LARP, and this was a LARP where I was a baby neonate with low status and barely any disciplines. But I did have Protean 2, so I had agg claws. Elders treated me like a baby tiger - sweet, you'd probably win if it decided to attack you, but you might get really hurt if it freaked the hell out. <br /> <br /> The same applies in Requiem to those Gangrel gifted with agg claws. But given that it requires Protean 4, no baby Gangrel is going to be rocking agg claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:29:01-08:00","id":1057255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1057249#post1057249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same applies in Requiem to those Gangrel gifted with agg claws. But given that it requires Protean 4, no baby Gangrel is going to be rocking agg claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Now that XP costs don't scale exponentially, 4 dots in one Discipline is fairly attainable for a neonate if they specialize. You won't be able to start play with agg claws unless you do Climbing the Ladder or otherwise start with XP &gt; 0, but it won't take you long to get them if they're your priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:31:14-08:00","id":1057292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1056070-claws-of-the-unholy-drawback?p=1057255#post1057255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno. Now that XP costs don't scale exponentially, 4 dots in one Discipline is fairly attainable for a neonate if they specialize. You won't be able to start play with agg claws unless you do Climbing the Ladder or otherwise start with XP &gt; 0, but it won't take you long to get them if they're your priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it is possible to achieve 4XP in 3 (+/-1) game sessions, assuming that a player makes risky actions or likes getting into trouble. As always it depends on the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,